// ─────────── value construction primitives ───────────
//
// value_make / list_make are type-erased compiler primitives.
// Surface type tags (Value(T1,...,Tn) / ValueList(T)) are checked before lowering;
// the IR carries no tag. Declared arity 0 — actual call-site arity is unbounded
// and enforced at the surface. §5b bootstrap identities.
//
// The registry format (fixed-arity FnGenesis) cannot express unbounded typed
// construction; these entries are intentionally under-specified here.
// Type checking is fully discharged at the surface before lowering reaches these.

// value_make: §5b identity = SHA-256("value_make")
fn value_make
  identity 0xf334e7070de9e3c1d96b5b5bf067a3cbe9ad00697911f1427626455d82242aee
  kind leaf
  in ()
  out Unit
  effect pure
  deterministic true
  idempotent true
end

